What the fork changes
---------------------

New code lives in app/src/main/java/com/limelight/strmqt/ and in resource
files whose names start with "strmqt". Edits to upstream files are kept
small, and are marked "StrmQt fork" where they are code:

- app/build.gradle: the application id (com.strmlight) and name, and JUnit
  for the fork's unit tests.
- app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml: the launcher entry moves from PcView to
  the fork's LaunchActivity; the fork's activities, boot receiver and wake
  service, and the permissions those need.
- Removed, since StrmLight streams StrmQt only: the host list (PcView), the
  app grid (AppView and the grid package), adding a computer by address
  (AddComputerManually), launcher and TV-channel shortcuts
  (ShortcutTrampoline, ShortcutHelper, TvChannelHelper, PosterContentProvider)
  and their layouts and icons. Game.java no longer reports shortcut use, and
  StreamSettings relaunches LaunchActivity instead of PcView.
- app/src/main/java/com/limelight/Game.java: hooks for remote mode and for
  handing an ended stream back to the launcher.
- app/src/main/res/xml/preferences.xml: a "StrmQt" settings category.
- app/src/main/res/values/styles.xml: the app theme takes StrmQt's colours
  (ground, surfaces, text, amber accent) and dialog theme, so upstream
  screens match the fork's.
- app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml also gives the fork's screens their
  theme and declares the setup preview's entry, enabled in debug builds
  only (app/src/debug/res/values/strmqt_bools.xml).
- app/src/main/res/mipmap-*/ic_launcher*.png, drawable-xhdpi/atv_banner.png,
  drawable/ic_channel.xml and values/ic_launcher_background.xml: the launcher
  icon and TV banner are replaced with artwork rendered from StrmQt's brand
  files (assets/brand in the StrmQt source). The banner wordmark is set in
  Archivo and IBM Plex Mono, both under the SIL Open Font License.

Brand assets and fonts
----------------------

StrmLight's own screens use StrmQt's look. These files come from, or are
drawn from, the StrmQt source:

- app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/strmqt_symbol.png: StrmQt's aperture
  symbol, rendered from assets/brand/strmqt-symbol.svg in the StrmQt source.
- app/src/main/res/drawable-xhdpi/atv_banner.png: the symbol and the
  StrmLight wordmark, drawn for this fork in the fonts below.

Fonts bundled unmodified in app/src/main/assets/fonts, each under the SIL
